  {F), L), R)} the reorientation achieved by the larvae.}}{9}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:4}{{4}{9}{\textbf {Zebrafish mutants for \emph {mtnr1ba}, \emph {mtnr1bb}, and \emph {mtnr1c} show normal responsiveness to Melatonin's effects on habituation learning}\\ Habituation behaviour comparing mutants for \emph {mtnr1ba} (\textbf {A-F}; 4 independent experiments: DMSO \emph {mtnr1ba\textsuperscript {+/?}} n~=~84, Melatonin \emph {mtnr1ba\textsuperscript {+/?}} n~=~366, DMSO \emph {mtnr1ba\textsuperscript {-/-}} n~=~26, Melatonin \emph {mtnr1ba\textsuperscript {-/-}} n~=~103), \emph {mtnr1bb} (\textbf {G-L}; 1 independent experiment: DMSO \emph {mtnr1bb\textsuperscript {+/?}} n~=~66, Melatonin \emph {mtnr1bb\textsuperscript {+/?}} n~=~171, DMSO \emph {mtnr1bb\textsuperscript {-/-}} n~=~9, Melatonin \emph {mtnr1bb\textsuperscript {-/-}} n~=~53), and \emph {mtnr1c} (\textbf {M-R}; 2 independent experiments: DMSO \emph {mtnr1c\textsuperscript {+/?}} n~=~91, Melatonin \emph {mtnr1c\textsuperscript {+/?}} n~=~347, DMSO \emph {mtnr1c\textsuperscript {-/-}} n~=~20, Melatonin \emph {mtnr1c\textsuperscript {-/-}} n~=~70) to their WT and heterozygous sibling controls. Larvae are treated with either \SI {1}{\micro \Molar } Melatonin, or vehicle (0.1DF stimuli are delivered at 1-minute intervals, in 4 blocks of 60 stimuli, separated by 1hr of rest (from 0:00-7:00). 1.5 hours later a block of 30 vibration stimuli are delivered at 1-minute intervals (\textbf {i}). Each dot is the probability of response to one DF. Lines are smoothed in time with a Savitzky–Golay filter (window = 15 stimuli, order = 2). Data is shown for the following behavioural components: \\ \textbf {A), G), M)} the probability of response to the stimulus: \\ \textbf {B), H), N)} the response latency, \\ \textbf {C), I), O)} the maximum tail-bend amplitude achieved during the movement, \\ \textbf {D), J), P)} the duration of the movement, \\ \textbf {E), K), Q)} the displacement of the movement, and \\ \textbf {F), L), R)} the reorientation achieved by the larvae}{figure.caption.14}{}}
